ScyllaDB Go Driver (2022)
How we built a driver that outperforms GoCQL and Rust
Tags: go, scylla, database, performance


Michał Matczuk

* Introduction
- New ScyllaDB Go Driver project
- Collaboration with University of Warsaw
- Goal: Exceed performance of both GoCQL and ScyllaDB Rust Driver
- Focus on "shared-nothing" architecture for maximum performance
- Featured on Hacker News front page twice

* Performance Highlights

Benchmark:
Insert 100 million rows concurrently, evenly distributed across cores.

- ~4x faster than GoCQL
- 2x faster than ScyllaDB Rust Driver
- 2x lower average latency under high concurrency

