* Frame Coalescing Optimization (kind of new)

- Key improvement: Brief waiting period to batch multiple frames
- Before: 36% of execution time spent in syscall.Write
- After: Only 7.5% of execution time spent in syscall.Write
- 2x performance improvement from this optimization alone

* Frame Coalescing Implementation (kind of new)

.code ../scylla-go-driver/transport/conn.go /func \(.*connWriter\) loop/,/^}/

* Query Routing: B-tree Improvement

- Standard data structure for token ring storage
- Addressed N+1 problem for slices
- Utilized Google's B-tree implementation
- Enhanced with Go generics
- Featured on Hacker News front page

.link https://www.scylladb.com/2022/04/27/shaving-40-off-googles-b-tree-implementation-with-go-generics/

* Query Routing Optimization (new)

- Pre-computing query plans instead of generating on-demand
- Eliminating allocations during connection selection
- Reduced connection selection time from 17% to 7.5% of total execution time
- Token-aware routing for partition-key optimization

* Query Routing Implementation

- Replaced B-tree with binary search over slice
- Implemented trie of nodes to store replica sets
- Store list of replicas for each token

.code ../scylla-go-driver/transport/trie.go /type trie struct/,/^}/

.code ../scylla-go-driver/transport/trie.go /func .* Next/,/^}/

* Query Routing Policy Interface

.code ../scylla-go-driver/transport/policy.go /type HostSelectionPolicy interface/,/^}/

    var local, remote []*Node
    pi := qi.topology.policyInfo
    if qi.tokenAware {
    	pos := pi.ring.tokenLowerBound(qi.token)
    	local = pi.ring[pos].localReplicas
    	remote = pi.ring[pos].remoteReplicas
    } else {
    	// Fallback to DC aware round robin on all nodes.
    	local = pi.localNodes
    	remote = pi.remoteNodes
    }
    if offset < len(local) {
    	idx := (qi.offset + uint64(offset)) % uint64(len(local))
    	return local[idx]
    } else if offset < len(local)+len(remote) {
    	idx := (qi.offset + uint64(offset) - uint64(len(local))) % uint64(len(remote))
    	return remote[idx]
    }

* Benchmarks

* Memory Allocation Comparison

- New driver: 0.68 allocations per insert
- GoCQL: 3.44 allocations per insert
- Rust driver: 0.91 allocations per insert

